{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/93665-very-much-off-topic-a-request-regarding-a-petition-against-discrimination","id":93665,"title":"Very much off topic: A request regarding a petition against discrimination","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-18T12:07:30-07:00","id":93665,"title":"Very much off topic: A request regarding a petition against discrimination","content":"Hopefully this is an acceptable topic, even given this is the off-topic thread. I usually do my best to not bring up religion or politics, but this topic is important enough to me to bring up both in one post. <br /> <br /> So, I'm sure that many of you are aware of more than a few states are attempting to pass bills that would legitimize and legalize discrimination if it is based on religious beliefs. Mississippi, my home state, has a bill like this that has already successfully passed the MS senate. I couldn't stand by and let it pass without at least attempting to do something about it. The White House provides a site where anyone can post a petition, and if a petition reaches at least 100,000 signatures then the White House will at least examine the petition and prepare a statement regarding it. I have created a petition asking for, at the very least, a statement from the White House denouncing this attempt to allow discrimination based on religious grounds. I'd like to ask any that read this at least take a look at the petition and consider signing it. If you do so, please spread the link to others you may know who are willing to add their signatures. It's not much, but I hope that it can make a difference no matter how small. Thanks for your time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://petitions.whitehouse.gov/petition/speak-out-against-ms-senate-bill-2681-ms-religious-freedom-restoration-act-and-similar-bills/KDcNCyKb\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://petitions.whitehouse.gov/petition/speak-out-against-ms-senate-bill-2681-ms-religious-freedom-restoration-act-and-similar-bills/KDcNCyKb\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://petitions.whitehouse.gov/petition/speak-out-against-ms-senate-bill-2681-ms-religious-freedom-restoration-act-and-similar-bills/KDcNCyKb\" target=\"_blank\"> https://petitions.whitehouse.gov/petition/speak-out-against-ms-senate-bill-2681-ms-religious-freedom-restoration-act-and-similar-bills/KDcNCyKb </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T13:45:20-07:00","id":93777,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that the bill is largely dead and in a &quot;review&quot; state.<br /> <br /> A federal petition, as you are encouraging, requires a response from the white house which would be &quot;We have already decided this particular matter is a state issue at this time&quot;. So... not exactly particularly useful. And the president and several federal representatives have already gone on record as saying they don't like such things... So I don't honestly see what you would stand to gain. You might see more progress by writing your state representatives and venting your views.<br /> <br /> In the unlikely event this actually passes (note I do consider this unlikely) I would expect this law to get slapped down in record time. I just read through the bill. Under the conditions of that bill it would be perfectly legal for me to declare myself christian and head to Mississippi and start building up a collection of slaves (race doesn't matter so I wonder if there are enough redheads to go around).<br /> <br /> On the plus side, unlike the recent Arizona bill the state authorities are *not* required to prevent federal authorities from stopping people stoning others for working on the Sabbath... it just prevents the state authorities from doing anything to stop me from doing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> So that tells me this bill (like the others) are in no way intended to actually pass. They're intended to score points for the people who proposed them with the heavily religious without ever actually being implemented or enforced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T09:58:37-07:00","id":95007,"title":"","content":"I wish I could agree with you, but the bill passed unanimously in the MS senate which is very troubling to hear. As far as what I hope this can accomplish? At the very least more people would be made aware of the bill and the blatant stupidity that is behind it. It's not much, but at least I tried to do something against it. I've written letters to both the senator and representative of my district, but an obviously canned response is the only thing that accomplished. Creating this petition may not change much at all, but I at least spoke out against this in as many ways possible.<br /> <br /> Given that, I hope it does pass at this point. I'll be first in line to utilize the protection that it gives, especially given the wording that offers protection not only for current acts, but even for those acts that might one day in the future hamper you. Seeing as I am ordained as a Reverend*, as are others I know, I look forward to sharing my deeply held beliefs with as many others that see fit to agree with me. It will certainly be nice to take full advantage of the protection this bill is offering as I plant acres of sacred drugs that God obviously provided to mankind to aid in the enlightenment of all his children. I'm sure we can give those redheads that God obviously gave you dominion over some good honest labor tending to the fields. I'll make sure to have the lawsuits prepared to file, since I feel that the state might impinge on my religious freedom at some point in the future. I'm sure a few million in damages and court costs is a small price for the state to pay to ensure that discrimination is OK, as long as it's based on your religion or lack thereof. <br /> <br /> *I'm ordained via the ULC, which is fully recognized by the state per a ruling by the MS Supreme Court, in the 70's(maybe the 80's). I made sure to verify that fact when I was asked to officiate a friends wedding.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}